Subject: [PATCH] feat(journey): stage discussion and attachments shared by
 staff and the portal

One thread per customer + lot + journey stage, stored in the EXISTING
quick_notes collection (kind=journey_note). Files go through the already
configured note byte store (core.inbox_attachments -> GridFS by default,
Drive only when configured); a failed store leaves no note and compensates
the bytes it wrote.

Permissions: staff with shipment_edit read and write both internal and
customer-visible content; a customer only ever sees CUSTOMER content on their
own lot and any content they write is forced to CUSTOMER. Attachment reads
re-prove the note, the tenant and the exact file id before any byte is read.

Wired into the shipment detail pane (staff) and below the customer journey map.
tests/test_journey_notes.py: 31 passed, including a real Streamlit AppTest post
+ reload on the customer portal and three mutations that fail the suite.
